  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "One Object on a Quiet Desk",
    "overview": "Etharic is one system with two registers. Every reading route (work, articles, about, 2026, contact) is a quiet desk: cool paper, graphite ink, hairline borders, Inter at reading sizes, flat surfaces. The homepage sets a single object on that desk: a split-flap board, a dark cased grid of hinged tiles like a station departures board. It shows the opening of the chosen audience's own sentence (\"i'm a finance student\") in Archivo glyphs; the intro directly under the board finishes the sentence. Choosing an audience makes every tile flip through its drum to the new character, and the characters take that audience's colour as they land.\n\nThe homepage hero is exactly one screen, one centred vertical axis: name, \"who's reading?\" and the audience switch, the board, the intro, one audience-specific action plus \"more about me\", and a small \"essays picked for you\" cue. Below the fold sit only the \"picked for\" heading, three hand-picked pieces of writing and a closing row. The audience is the only variable. Selecting one recolours the switch indicator, the primary action, the intro underlines and the \"picked for\" underline together, and flips the board, so the whole axis shifts at once.\n\nThe voice is personal and playful (lowercase copy, code-like intro lines, a pixel dog, a live clock) but the surfaces are restrained. The board is the one rendered object, a satin dark casing with matte tiles; everything around it is flat. Rejected: corporate polish, glossy neon 3D, glass, decorative gradients and glow halos.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Flat tonal surfaces with 1px hairlines; no elevation shadows outside the 3D board.",
      "One audience accent live at a time on the homepage, carried by a single variable with its own on-colour.",
      "Inter for everything readable; Archivo expanded only for the homepage name, the board's glyphs and the \"picked for\" heading.",
      "The hero is one screen on a single centred column; the board is decorative and its text is also in the page as plain text.",
      "Motion is short and ease-out; the board flips fast with a gravity fall, staggered across the grid, then stops rendering; reduced motion changes the characters at once."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Voice Rule",
        "body": "One audience accent is live at a time, and every accent-bearing element reads it through the shared variable, never a fixed audience colour. If an element should not change with the audience, it is not accent-coloured.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Paired Ink Rule",
        "body": "An accent fill always takes the on-colour paired with it, never a fixed white. Light accents (marigold, jade) carry graphite ink.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Ink-Only Board Rule",
        "body": "The audience reaches the board through its characters alone. Tiles, split line and casing stay neutral black for every audience; the accent fill never paints a tile.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Archivo Fence Rule",
        "body": "Archivo appears only on the homepage name, the board's glyphs and the homepage \"picked for\" heading. Any other text, including the intro, the switch, the picks cue and the cards, is Inter.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
